===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|Mach's conjecture}}

===Etymology===
Named after [[German]] [[physicist]] {{w|Ernst Mach}}, to whom the hypothesis is often attributed. Coined by {{w|Albert Einstein}}, who adopted the hypothesis and incorporated into his theory of [[general relativity]].

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[Mach]]'s [[principle]]}}

# {{lb|en|physics}} The principle that the [[inertia]] of a [[body]] arises from its [[relation]] to the [[totality]] of all other bodies in the [[universe]].

